  "english": "[Hymn: \"Angel of Your...\"]. Eve of the Fast of Saint James.\n17. Sunday. Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 3 [third Voice / GA]: \"Glorified Son.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]: \"You who are above.\"\n23. Saturday. Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]. Of David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n24. Sunday. Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]: \"Pre-eternal.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]: \"Your Resurrection,\" and \"Accepting, and our...\"\n29. Friday. Tone 3 [second Voice / BZ]. Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Saturday. Tone 4 [second Plagal / BK]. Fast. Of Basil the Patriarch, and the others.\n31. Sunday. Tone 5 [third Voice / GZ]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fast. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [third Voice / GZ]: \"Glorified is Your Resurrection,\" to the end. And see the others according to the order.\n\nJanuary [or December error in source, listing saint feasts of late November/December]:\n1. Monday [actually: and of Bishop Myron?]. Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]. Fast. Father [Hymn] of Fasting Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]: \"Blessed are You, Lord God of our fathers.\"\n5. Friday [actually: 25th?]. Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]. Of Bishop Myron. Martyrs [Hymn] in place: \"They marveled.\" Midday Hymn [Sharakan]: \"Who with light.\"\n26. Sunday. Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]. First [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]: \"Who for our salvation.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]: \"Arisen,\" and \"Wonderful.\"\n27. Monday. Tone 3 [second Voice / BZ]. Of Julian and Vasilis. Father [Hymn] Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]: \"Holy God, Creator.\" And the rest according to the order.\n\nDecember:\n3. Sunday. Tone 1 [first Voice / AZ]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 3 [second Voice / BZ]: \"Incorruptible.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [first Voice / AZ]: \"Who ineffably.\"\n4. Monday. Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]. Of Gennadius and Mercurius, and of Jacob and Iraparish [Iraphara].\n5. Tuesday. Tone 3 [second Voice / BZ]. Of King Abgar. The Scripture reading and Gospel are those of Theodosius.\n6. Wednesday. Tone 4 [second Plagal / BK]. Father [Hymn] Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]: \"Truly.\"\n9. Saturday. Tone 5 [third Voice / GZ]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n10. Sunday. Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]. Third [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 4 [second Plagal / BK]: \"Without beginning, God.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]: [incipit abbreviated].\n\nRoman Weekly Cycle 6:\n19. Wednesday. Tone 3 [second Voice / BZ]. Father [Hymn] of Fasting Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]: \"Glorified forever.\"\n20. Thursday. Tone 4 [second Plagal / BK]. Of King Theodosius and the Holy Children of Ephesus.\n22. Saturday. Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]. Of Athanasius and Cyril the Patriarchs.\n23. Sunday. Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]. Second [Sunday]. Father [Hymn] Tone 4 [second Plagal / BK]: \"By Your will You came.\" Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]: \"The Resurrection of the Son of God.\"\n24. Monday. Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]. Of Cyriacus and Julitta, and of Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Father [Hymn] Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]: \"Holy God, Creator.\"\n\nJanuary:\n6. Thursday. Tone 6 [third Plagal / GK]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The period of non-fasting [eating] is thirty-nine days.\n15. Saturday. Tone 7 [fourth Plagal / DZ]. Of John the Forerunner.\n16. Sunday. Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]. First [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [fourth Plagal / DK]: \"The hosts of angels.\"\n17. Monday. Tone 1 [first Voice / AZ]. Of Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n18. Tuesday. Tone 2 [first Plagal / AK]. Of Antony, and Triphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.",
